<title>USA: P-Com wins $16.5 million contract.</title>
<headline>P-Com wins $16.5 million contract.</headline>
<dateline>CAMPBELL, Calif. 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>P-Com Inc said it reached an agreement valued in excess of $16.5 million, to supply additional digital millimeter wave radio systems to Advanced Radio Telecom.</p>
<p>Advanced Radio provides wireless broadband network services for the transmission of voice, video and high-speed data. It has been granted Federal Communications Commission licenses to operate advanced wireless microwave systems in more than 60 metropolitan markets throughout the United States and has applications pending in an additional 100 markets, R-Com said.</p>
</text>
